\f1\fs22 Shakti found her first.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Ah, Superintendent Lanning. What wonderfully propitious timing. I could have the scriptwriters knock up a part for you in this scene, if you like. Consider it a little favour. From me, to you.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What\'92s going on here?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93
\f2\i What\'92s going on here?
\f1\i0 \'94 Alexander mocked. \'93Well, yes, I suppose that could be a good line, but let\'92s address your character motivation. Really, is that what you\'92d ask as lead investigator?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander never failed to interrupt Hayley\'92s mental circuits, and she needed a moment to reboot her sanity.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Let me set the scene for you. This is Chantara\'92s compound,\'94 he said, like explaining to a five-year-old, \'93where he holds Sarah Jacobson captive. We\'92re here to rescue Sarah, and re-apprehend Chantara.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And PAPER? I hear gun-ships up there.\'94 Hayley looked up, as if expecting the Layer to part and a dozen angry gunships to level their particle weapons straight at her.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Oh, they\'92re just extras, detective. We have to ratchet up the tension a bit, and it\'92s always good to share a roller coaster. I\'92m sure you know how it is among secret service siblings.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley nodded\'97the tension was indeed ratcheted. \'93I\'92m going in.\'94 She strode to the gate, where six Elvi guards in camo ponchos and capes eyed her like a pest they weren\'92t quite allowed to poison.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander hurried after her. \'93Now is not the time for improv, detective. No telling how Chanta might respond.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley spun on him. \'93And what exactly is your relationship with 
\f2\i Chanta
\f1\i0  Chantara?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander chewed this for a while. \'93No relationship at all, detective.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Other than all the crime-scene clean ups you tossed Enchanted Cleaning Services\'92 way.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I don\'92t know where your production team finds their research, but I can assure you\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Tell me about the Travis Teh murder.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Travis Teh 
\f2\i suicide
\f1\i0 , detective.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Your stamp on the file doesn\'92t make it so.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Look, detective, if you\'92d let me explain the story arcs we\'92re developing\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Tax the taxing story arcs, lieutenant, I just want the truth.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The truth?\'94 Alexander sniffed, and found the concept unpleasant.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Tony Chantara is no terrorist.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You\'92re reading off the wrong script, detective. I\'92ve already counselled you, as any good mentor would: get your own show. Chantara\'92s strictly in my story, detective\'97a small supporting part. So if I say he\'92s a terrorist, then he is. Chantara kidnapped Sarah from the Stickett Inn, just before he blew it up.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Are you aware Sarah Jacobson went to the Stickett Inn to meet Tony Chantara? They were on a date\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Impossible!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93According to witnesses, Sarah came to pick him up. They were going out to dinner.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Chantara? And\'85\'94 Alexander failed to summon Sarah\'92s name. \'93I\'92d have known if Tony\'85\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley raised an eyebrow as he trailed off. \'93How would you know? Because he\'92d tell you? Because you\'92re friends\'97isn\'92t that right?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I contract his cleaning services, that is all. At work, he often blathers about his personal life. Did you know his longtime girlfriend, Andrea\'97pretty little thing, no class, a little too sassy\'97just dumped him and took allocation with another man?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley let that pass. \'93Are you aware the Stickett Inn wasn\'92t the first time Chantara and Jacobson had met?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander became appallingly apoplectic. \'93He\'92s Cloudborne, detective. Why would an Airborne like Sarah Jacobson bother with a Cloudborne cleaner?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley dug an evidence bag from her tote and held it out. The contents: a pack of mostly pink satin boxer shorts. \'93I dunno. But she was buying him underwear.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93That\'92s preposterous.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Is it? I found these in Sarah\'92s apartment\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Have you no respect for the kidnapped?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93They\'92re exactly the same design I found in Chantara\'92s place.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You\'92re tainting crime scenes, now?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93At least I visit crime scenes.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander snatched the bag and squinted at the contents. \'93Hah! Floormart. If a dozen production assistants dropped their daks right now, many of them would be wearing Floormart Reg Grundies.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I also found an expensive overnight bag: clothes\'97women\'92s clothes.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I always knew Chantara was a deviant.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Airborne clothes.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93He stole them.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And high-end bandages and medications in the bathroom. Likely for treating Chantara\'92s burns.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Stole those, too.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The bathroom was spotless.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander initially had no retort, then: \'93He\'92s a cleaner, detective.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>To Hayley, that observation was almost credible, but she had more. \'93Chantara and Jacobson spoke together earlier that day, before the bombing.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93When?\'94 Alexander demanded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sarah Jacobson started a new job that morning, in the same office where Travis Teh was murdered.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93
\f2\i Suicided
\f1\i0 ,\'94 Alexander corrected. \'93Wait\'97what?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Witnesses place her and Chantara together twice that day: once, while Chantara was cleaning Teh\'92s office, then again later in Sarah\'92s office.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What could they possibly have to discuss?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Dinner plans?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander nearly choked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley pressed on. \'93Also: PAPER sent an agent to the Teh crime scene not long after Chantara left.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The blood drained from Alexander\'92s face. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I thought that might get your attention. As the agent searched Teh\'92s office, Jacobson confronted him, and there was quite the scene before the agent stormed off muttering\'85\'94 Hayley checked her notes. \'93\'85\'91the cleaner has the documents, the cleaner has the documents.\'92 Do you have any idea what documents he meant? Of course you don\'92t. You didn\'92t even bother with a cursory investigation.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93If PAPER was chasing Chantara that morning, it confirms he\'92s a terrorist.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>While Hayley rolled her eyes, a ground car pulled up and a woman stepped out. Hayley studied her, intrigued. She carried an oversized crocheted tote; there was a flower in her hair, and she wore what appeared to be a tie-dyed lab coat. Hayley groped for a category, and came up with: a cross between a hippy, a hair model, and a biology professor you\'92d try not to perv on in a staff meeting. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Who is this?\'94 Alexander scanned around in panic. \'93Jason! Jason! What taxing page are we on? Someone give me a script!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As Alexander blustered away, Hayley watched the pervable professor approach the gates. The guards stepped aside and let her through.
